wer Saxony, Germany, in the Oldenburg Münsterland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/clos-de-vougeot"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/clos-de-vougeot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Clos de Vougeot</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Clos de Vougeot is a walled vineyard of about 50 hectares in the Côte de Nuits, Burgundy, created by the monks of Cîteaux Abbey from the early twelfth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/closure-of-the-neoplatonic-academy"><span class="enc-name">Closure of the Neoplatonic Academy</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The closure of the Neoplatonic Academy refers to the Byzantine emperor Justinian's measures in 529 CE that ended pagan philosophical teaching in Athens.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/clotilda-slave-ship"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/clotilda-slave-ship.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Clotilda</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Clotilda was a two-masted schooner and the last known American slave ship to bring enslaved Africans to the United States, landing 110 men, women and children at…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/clough-oughter-castle"><span class="enc-name">Clough Oughter Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Clough Oughter Castle is a ruined circular tower on a small island in Lough Oughter, County Cavan, Ireland, built in the early 13th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cloves"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cloves.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cloves</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Cloves are the aromatic dried flower buds of a tree native to the Maluku Islands of Indonesia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/clovis-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Clovis I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Clovis I was king of the Franks in the late fifth and early sixth centuries and founder of the Merovingian dynasty.</span></a></li></ul>
